th a $318M market cap on $187M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at -33% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $25M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -10.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 40% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 27% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (92% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.077},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 64% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 381% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Public Policy (PPHC) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/what-public-policy-pphc-said-on-its-q3-earnings-call.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794478431.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.778,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Contrasting Public Policy (PPHC) and Its Competitors","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/contrasting-public-policy-pphc-and-its-competitors.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794338157.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.844,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"PPHC reaffirms 2026 outlook of $213M-$216M revenue and $48.5M-$50.5M adjusted EBITDA while adding new $105M credit facility (NASDAQ:PPHC)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4669448-pphc-reaffirms-2026-outlook-of-213m-216m-revenue-and-48_5m-50_5m-adjusted-ebitda-while-adding","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794281622.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Public Policy (PPHC) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/public-policy-pphc-q3-2026-004540000.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794272011.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"PPHC Announces N